businesses continue to clean up damage  from the weekend demonstrations Kristen  Drummond is live at a gas station at  Koval and Tropicana where a store there  was looted as we brought you last night  at 11:00 Kristin yes Brian we are right  across the street from the rubble store  as you can see behind me plywood now  does cover a window metro police tell us  that several people from the strip  protest came here they set trash on fire  got into a fight and then staff tell us  today that they were looted they did not  tell us how much were taken or what was  taken however this was not the only  place in the valley damaged last night a  few stores at the Las Vegas North  Premium Outlets were broken into some  businesses were closed for the day while  others decided to board up the windows  as a precaution now crosstown Metro  sources say a group of people through  several Malte cocktails at the front  windows of a colles buy Charleston and  Nellis damage appears minimal and  customers were still able to shop there  today but the destruction is frustrating  to those who want to keep the community  safe and the demonstrations to remain  peaceful I kind of wonder sometimes is  it all you know these so-called  protesters that aren't even a part of  the solution you know it's the question  of are they trying to be a part of a  solution or a part of the problem  cleanup is still happening in downtown  Las Vegas city maintenance crews and  volunteers continue removing graffiti  after demonstrators tag businesses and  property during Saturday's protests  metro police did make several arrests  yesterday as well as at the outlet mall  reporting live Kristin Drummond 8 News  now
 

